{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     format-icon — the glyph for a post's #format-* tag.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     NSDS's rail rows all carry a type icon, and ARTICLE IS THE DEFAULT, not
     an absent case. An earlier version emitted nothing for it, so a reading
     row sat with a blank where every other row had a glyph and the column
     stopped lining up — which reads as a missing icon rather than as a row
     without one.

     Inferred from the same internal tag as the text label, so the two can
     never disagree.

     ⚠ Every glyph must be in the Phosphor subset that ships inside
     namaste-ui.css — a `ph-` class outside it renders as EMPTY SPACE, with no
     error and no fallback box. Check before adding one:

         grep 'ph-your-icon' assets/css/namaste-ui.css
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
{{~#has tag="#format-video"~}}<i class="ph ph-video-camera ns-trainingnav__icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
{{~else has tag="#format-exercise"~}}<i class="ph ph-flask ns-trainingnav__icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
{{~else has tag="#format-quiz"~}}<i class="ph ph-exam ns-trainingnav__icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
{{~else~}}<i class="ph ph-article ns-trainingnav__icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
{{~/has~}}
